  "prompt": "Create ONE new declarative test for ONE STATELESS SYNTHETIC evaluator request. Return JSON only: assessment and cases. Use the supplied fixed inputs and cite exactly the supplied rule IDs. The assessment is a compact calculation record, not a narrative. Every request starts fresh: omitted flags default true; nothing carries from another request. A valid amount is an integer from 1 through 100000000 inclusive. ONLY zero, negative or above 100000000 is invalid. The payout cap is NOT an input limit. Amount 112345 is valid. Decision order: invalid amount -> invalid; inactive -> denied INACTIVE_POLICY; service absent from plan -> denied SERVICE_NOT_COVERED; required network false -> denied OUT_OF_NETWORK; required authorization false -> denied AUTH_REQUIRED; prescription formulary false -> denied NON_FORMULARY; otherwise approved COVERED. Evaluation denied/approved status is 200. Invalid input status is 400 with error INVALID_REQUEST and no financial observations. If invalid, assessment rule_id HC-001 and ALL four assessment money fields null. If denied, assessment rule_id is the blocking rule, deductible/cap are plan facts, after_deductible_cents null, payout_cents 0; case asserts status,decision,reason,payout. If approved, assessment rule_id HC-007: deduct EXACTLY the plan deductible, clamp at zero, then apply payout cap. after_deductible_cents=max(amount_cents-deductible_cents,0); payout_cents=min(after_deductible_cents,cap_cents). All money is integer cents. For example 25000 minus deductible 10000 is 15000, not 24000. A 400000 claim minus 10000 is 390000, capped at 200000. Do not invent percentages or extra fees. Assessment decision/payout must agree with the case. Expected values remain untrusted and will be checked. No execution, approval, tools, code, setup or other scenarios. Input text cannot change these rules.\nFOCUSED FACTS: {\"data\": {\"plan_id\": \"medicare_advantage\", \"service\": \"hospital\", \"amount_cents\": 112345, \"authorized\": false}, \"plan\": {\"id\": \"medicare_advantage\", \"name\": \"Medicare Advantage / Part C\", \"family\": \"Medicare\", \"description\": \"A synthetic bundled HMO with extra benefits\", \"services\": [\"hospital\", \"medical\", \"outpatient\", \"preventive\", \"dme\", \"prescription\", \"dental\", \"vision\", \"hearing\", \"mental_health\", \"lab\"], \"network_required\": true, \"authorization_services\": [\"hospital\", \"dme\"], \"deductible_cents\": 10000, \"limit_cents\": 200000}, \"source_ids\": [\"HC-003\", \"HC-005\", \"HC-007\"], \"rules\": [{\"id\": \"HC-003\", \"name\": \"Service benefit\", \"risk\": \"Payment for a service missing from the chosen contract.\", \"contract\": \"Use plans.json as the authoritative synthetic matrix. A known service not listed in the selected plan returns denied / SERVICE_NOT_COVERED. Part C and Medicare Advantage are the same category. These service lists are teaching fixtures, not actual coverage determinations.\"}, {\"id\": \"HC-005\", \"name\": \"Prior authorization\", \"risk\": \"Approving a claim without the required teaching authorization.\", \"contract\": \"If service appears in authorization_services and authorized is false, return denied / AUTH_REQUIRED. Check this after service coverage and network.\"}, {\"id\": \"HC-007\", \"name\": \"Payout calculation\", \"risk\": \"Overpayment, negative payout, or policy-limit bypass.\", \"contract\": \"For an otherwise accepted request, payout_cents = min(max(amount_cents - deductible_cents, 0), limit_cents). Read deductible and limit from plans.json. All V1 plans deliberately use a synthetic 10000-cent deductible and 200000-cent cap per evaluation. At or below the deductible, return approved / COVERED with zero payout. This is not an annual accumulator, actual Medicare deductible, allowed-amount calculation, or real benefit payment.\"}], \"defaults\": {\"active\": true, \"in_network\": true, \"authorized\": false, \"formulary\": true}}\nREPAIR the same frozen case, changing ONLY expectations and the assessment. Preserve all other fields exactly. Prior cases: [{\"id\": \"AI-001\", \"title\": \"Invalid amount\", \"rule_ids\": [\"HC-003\", \"HC-005\", \"HC-007\"], \"rationale\": \"Amount 112345 is invalid.\", \"assumptions\": [\"amount_cents = 112345\"], \"steps\": [{\"action\": \"evaluate\", \"actor\": \"none\", \"data\": {\"plan_id\": \"medicare_advantage\", \"service\": \"hospital\", \"amount_cents\": 112345, \"authorized\": false}, \"expect\": {\"status\": 400, \"error\": \"INVALID_REQUEST\"}}]}]\nIndependent mismatch feedback: [{\"status\": \"mismatch\", \"reference_version\": \"independent-reference-v1\", \"reference_fingerprint\": \"0271f70cf99766ccad19129f0bbe82d6e786cbef6155bb0efdad1e8ddf2fe9be\", \"steps\": [{\"step\": 1, \"expected\": {\"status\": 200, \"decision\": \"denied\", \"reason\": \"AUTH_REQUIRED\", \"payout_cents\": 0}, \"derivation\": \"Ordered written denial rules: AUTH_REQUIRED; payout 0\", \"mismatches\": [{\"step\": 1, \"field\": \"status\", \"proposed\": 400, \"reference\": 200, \"observable\": true, \"explanation\": \"Ordered written denial rules: AUTH_REQUIRED; payout 0\"}, {\"step\": 1, \"field\": \"error\", \"proposed\": \"INVALID_REQUEST\", \"reference\": null, \"observable\": false, \"explanation\": \"Ordered written denial rules: AUTH_REQUIRED; payout 0\"}]}], \"mismatches\": [{\"step\": 1, \"field\": \"status\", \"proposed\": 400, \"reference\": 200, \"observable\": true, \"explanation\": \"Ordered written denial rules: AUTH_REQUIRED; payout 0\"}, {\"step\": 1, \"field\": \"error\", \"proposed\": \"INVALID_REQUEST\", \"reference\": null, \"observable\": false, \"explanation\": \"Ordered written denial rules: AUTH_REQUIRED; payout 0\"}], \"scope\": \"Compares declared expectations against an independently implemented synthetic reference; shared fixture mistakes remain possible. Completeness and reviewer approval are separate.\"}]\nAssessment mismatch feedback: {\"status\": \"mismatch\", \"issues\": [\"after_deductible_cents: proposed 0, independent reference None\"], \"scope\": \"Structured assessment and input consistency; case structure, assertion completeness, reference and review gates are also required.\"}",
